A typical function-calling request declares a schema alongside the prompt; the model returns a structured call instead of prose:

```json
{
  "tools": [{
    "name": "get_weather",
    "parameters": {
      "city": { "type": "string" },
      "unit": { "type": "string", "enum": ["celsius", "fahrenheit"] }
    }
  }],
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Weather in Lisbon, in celsius?" }]
}
```

Expected model output — not prose, a structured call your code executes directly:

```json
{ "name": "get_weather", "arguments": { "city": "Lisbon", "unit": "celsius" } }
```
